  "body": "## Exact negative answer\nClaimed solved after one substantive author turn for the unmodified source implication: dropping beta_2>0 while retaining strict positivity on the ordinary critical cone does not preserve strong L2-squared growth.\n\nThe exact defocusing critical-wave example has a genuine unique global optimizer, positive sparsity/state penalties and a positive constant control radius. Its critical cone is explicitly {0}, which the source permits. Feasible pulses converge in L-infinity while their objective gap divided by squared L2 distance tends to zero. This addresses both the report's L2 neighborhood and the full preprint's L-infinity version, including the optional terminal velocity term.\n\nA further theorem disproves a natural Lipschitz L2-control estimate under terminal-target perturbations. No assertion is made that every beta_2=0 theory, stronger sufficient condition or weaker stability estimate fails.\n\n## Review and reproducibility\nSeparate full analytic/source review passed the unchanged proof with no correction. All3,937 author exact controls replay identically;1,385 separate controls pass. The global minimum, critical-cone vacuity, nonlinear remainder, compactness and source topology were reviewed mathematically, not inferred from finite tests. Classical PDE inputs are credited; no historical novelty or human peer review is claimed.\n\nOnly this target's QUEUE row changes to claimed_solved1/5. The exact frozen author packet and seven portable review files are included; source PDFs and full reading copies are excluded.",
